[node name="OptionButton" type="OptionButton" parent="." unique_id=1237191194]
z_index = 10
offset_left = 1079.0
offset_top = 691.0
offset_right = 1237.0
offset_bottom = 722.0
tooltip_text = "Fitness evolution across generations.

Mean fitness is the arithmetic mean of the fitness values of all agents
in a generation.

Best fitness is the highest individual fitness obtained in that
generation.

Higher values indicate better overall performance under the current
simulation's fitness function."
theme = SubResource("Theme_5bjn8")

[node name="OptionButton2" type="OptionButton" parent="." unique_id=525999736]
z_index = 10
offset_left = 1079.0
offset_top = 842.0
offset_right = 1237.0
offset_bottom = 873.0
tooltip_text = "Genetic diversity is the mean normalized Hamming distance between all
pairs of genomes in the population.

For genomes g_i and g_j of length L, their normalized Hamming distance is

d(g_i,g_j) = (1/L) * sum_k [g_i(k) != g_j(k)].

The population diversity is the mean of d(g_i,g_j) over all unordered
pairs of agents.

A value of 0 means all genomes are identical. A value of 1 means every
compared pair differs at every gene position.

For the complete genome used here, L = 568 gene digits.

Diversity      Mean differing gene digits per pair
1                  568       (all gene digits different)
1e-1           56.8
1e-2           5.68
1e-3           0.568
0                  0         (all genomes identical)

The values are pairwise averages, so the number of differing digits
does not need to be an integer."
mouse_filter = 1
theme = SubResource("Theme_qux5w")

[node name="Title2" type="Label" parent="." unique_id=1660812460]
offset_left = 35.0
offset_top = 547.0
offset_right = 360.0
offset_bottom = 581.0
tooltip_text = "This heatmap shows the relation between  
two selected genes and agent fitness.

Each axis represents one selected gene. 
Gene values are ordered using a
quaternary Gray code. Nearby positions 
therefore tend to represent small genetic 
changes.

Each cell contains the mean fitness
of all agents that fell into that bin.
Data from all generations in the
current simulation are accumulated.

The color scale is fixed from -1 to 1.
Bright pink cells have no samples yet.

Changing either gene selector rebuilds
the heatmap from the stored history.
"
mouse_filter = 1
theme = SubResource("Theme_sx4as")
theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0.8862745, 0.15686275, 0.15686275, 1)
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 18
text = "Genetic x Fitness Landscape"

